    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by platoon advantages and top-of-order security. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.03) anchor the outfield as our strongest plays, both benefiting from ideal leadoff positioning and high-leverage platoon matchups against right-handed pitching. **Yelich** faces McGreevy with a 13% efficiency boost, while **Crow-Armstrong** leverages an elite park factor and dynamic platoon advantage against Kremer, reinforcing the need to chase stolen base upside early in the rotation. **Josh Smith** (64.66) and **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) round out the high-efficiency core; both are hitting in the two-hole, providing the best path to volume-driven scoring despite the varied skill levels of their opposing starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's board involved **Casey Schmitt**, who provided a respectable 43.03 efficiency score but failed to displace the higher-upside profiles like **Carson Benge** (43.82). While **Schmitt** benefits from a dynamic platoon boost, he is facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Cease, which dragged his projection below our threshold for starting confidence. Consequently, **Schmitt** remains on the bench alongside **Nelson Velazquez**\u2014whose elite xwOBA (0.420) was neutralized by a tough matchup against Harrison\u2014and **Lars Nootbaar**, whose 35.14 score signals a clear \"below floor\" status for tonight. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the presence of elite arms like Cease and Kremer, though **Yordan Alvarez** (60.44) remains a must-start despite the platoon disadvantage against Griffin; his elite 0.475 xwOBA ensures he maintains a \"Strong\" rating regardless of the matchup. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (63.19) is a watch-item against the veteran Cole. Though the park factor penalizes him slightly, the combination of his three-hole protection and dynamic platoon split suggests he is well-positioned to drive in the runs necessary to keep the Zebras competitive in the 5x5 hunt. Keep an eye on weather reports for all East Coast matchups as the only remaining variable that could disrupt these optimized scores.",
